},{"words":[{"surface":"நலம்","parts":[{"text":"நலம்","lemma":"nalam","gloss":"goodness/beauty"}],"gloss":"goodness"},{"surface":"சால்","parts":[{"text":"சால்","lemma":"cāl","gloss":"abundant/great"}],"gloss":"abundant"},{"surface":"விழுப்பொருள்","parts":[{"text":"விழு","lemma":"viḻu","gloss":"excellent/precious"},{"text":"பொருள்","lemma":"poruḷ","gloss":"wealth"}],"gloss":"precious wealth"},{"surface":"பணிந்து","parts":[{"text":"பணி","lemma":"paṇi","gloss":"bow/submit"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"having done"}],"gloss":"humbly"},{"surface":"கொடுப்பினும்","parts":[{"text":"கொடு","lemma":"koṭu","gloss":"give"},{"text":"ப்பின்","lemma":"ppiṉ","gloss":"even if"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even if given"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புரையர்","parts":[{"text":"புரை","lemma":"purai","gloss":"greatness/worthiness"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"ar","gloss":"they (honorific/plural)"}],"gloss":"worthy ones"},{"surface":"அல்லோர்","parts":[{"text":"அல்","lemma":"al","gloss":"not"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"they"}],"gloss":"those who are not"},{"surface":"வரையலள்","parts":[{"text":"வரை","lemma":"varai","gloss":"marry"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"al","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அள்","lemma":"aḷ","gloss":"she"}],"gloss":"she will not marry"},{"surface":"இவள்","parts":[{"text":"இவள்","lemma":"ivaḷ","gloss":"she"}],"gloss":"she"},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"saying/thinking"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தந்தையும்","parts":[{"text":"தந்தையும்","lemma":"தந்தையும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொடாஅன்","parts":[{"text":"கொடாஅன்","lemma":"கொடாஅன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"ஆயின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"_","parts":[{"text":"_","lemma":"_","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வந்தோர்","parts":[{"text":"வந்தோர்","lemma":"வந்தோர்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"வாய்ப்ப","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"vāy","gloss":"succeed/fit"},{"text":"ப்ப","lemma":"ppa","gloss":"infinitival suffix"}],"gloss":"to fit/succeed"},{"surface":"இறுத்த","parts":[{"text":"இறு","lemma":"iṟu","gloss":"pitch/place"},{"text":"த்த","lemma":"tta","gloss":"past adjectival participle"}],"gloss":"pitched/placed"},{"surface":"ஏணி","parts":[{"text":"ஏணி","lemma":"ēṇi","gloss":"ladder"}],"gloss":"ladders"},{"surface":"ஆயிடை","parts":[{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"that"},{"text":"இடை","lemma":"iṭai","gloss":"place"}],"gloss":"in that place"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வருந்தின்று","parts":[{"text":"வருந்தின்று","lemma":"வருந்தின்று","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"கொல்லோ","lemma":"கொல்லோ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தானே_பருந்துஉயிர்த்து","parts":[{"text":"தானே_பருந்துஉயிர்த்து","lemma":"தானே_பருந்துஉயிர்த்து","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"இடை","parts":[{"text":"இடை","lemma":"iṭai","gloss":"middle"}],"gloss":"middle"},{"surface":"மதில்","parts":[{"text":"மதில்","lemma":"matil","gloss":"wall"}],"gloss":"wall"},{"surface":"சேக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"சே","lemma":"cē","gloss":"roost/rest"},{"text":"க்கும்","lemma":"kkum","gloss":"habitual/adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"resting/roosting"},{"surface":"புரிசை","parts":[{"text":"புரிசை","lemma":"puricai","gloss":"rampart/fortress wall"}],"gloss":"rampart"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"படை","parts":[{"text":"படை","lemma":"paṭai","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"armies"},{"surface":"மயங்கு","parts":[{"text":"மயங்கு","lemma":"mayaṅku","gloss":"clash/mingle"}],"gloss":"clashing"},{"surface":"ஆர்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ār","gloss":"difficult"}],"gloss":"difficult"},{"surface":"இடை","parts":[{"text":"இடை","lemma":"iṭai","gloss":"path/place"}],"gloss":"path"},{"surface":"நெடு","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"neṭu","gloss":"long/great"}],"gloss":"great"},{"surface":"நல்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"nal","gloss":"good/fine"}],"gloss":"fine"},{"surface":"ஊரே","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ūr","gloss":"town"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"town indeed"}]}],"literal":"Having bartered fish and heaped paddy, / the boats on top confuse the houses, / with bags of black pepper surrounding the houses, / the noisy shore gets stirred, / the gold brought by ships / is brought to shore by backwater boats, / mountain produce and sea produce / gathering together and giving to those who come, / Kuttuvan of the golden garland and abundant water-like toddy, / whose Muciri is like the roaring sea-drum, / even if precious wealth of abundant goodness is humbly given, / saying 'she will not marry those who are not worthy', / her father too does not give her, then... / the ladders pitched to succeed in that place, / did they suffer indeed? / where kites sigh and roost on the middle walls of the ramparts, / in the great fine town of difficult paths where armies clash.","translation":"In Muciri, the port city of Kuttuvan who wears golden garlands and pours out toddy like water, where the roaring sea sounds like a drum, fish is bartered for heaps of paddy, boats crowd the front yards of houses, bags of black pepper fill the homes, and the bustling shore is filled with noise. There, boats bring ashore the gold brought by ships, and the riches of the mountains and the seas are gathered and given freely to all who come. Even if suitors humbly offer precious wealth of great value, her father refuses to give her hand, saying she will not marry those who are not worthy. Because of this, the ladders pitched by the suitors to scale the fort walls must have suffered indeed, in this great, fine town of difficult paths where clashing armies meet, and kites sigh as they roost on the ramparts.","modern":"மீனை விற்று நெல்லைக் குவித்து, படகுகள் வீடுகளின் முன்னே வந்து குழப்பமடையச் செய்து, வீடுகளில் மிளகு மூட்டைகள் நிறைந்து கிடக்க, ஆரவாரமான கடற்கரை கலங்கிக் கிடக்கிறது. கப்பல்கள் கொண்டு வந்த பொன்னைத் தோணிகள் மூலம் கரைக்குக் கொண்டு வந்து சேர்க்கின்றனர். மலையின் வளங்களையும் கடலின் வளங்களையும் ஒன்றாகச் சேர்த்து வருவோர்க்கெல்லாம் வாரி வழங்கும், நீர் போன்ற கள்ளையும் பொன் மாலையையும் உடைய குட்டுவனின் முழங்கும் கடல் போன்ற முசிறிப் பட்டினத்தைப் போல, நலம் மிக்கப் பெரும் செல்வத்தைப் பணிந்து கொடுத்தாலும், 'இவள் தகுதியற்றவர்களுக்கு உரியவள் அல்லள்' என்று கூறித் தந்தை அவளைத் தர மறுக்கிறான். அதனால், போர்க்களத்தில் படைகள் மோதும் அரிய வழிகளைக் கொண்ட இப்பெரிய நல்ல ஊரில், பருந்துகள் பெருமூச்சு விட்டுக்கொண்டு மதில்களின் மேல் தங்கும் கோட்டைச் சுவர்களில், ஏறுவதற்காகப் பொருத்தப்பட்ட ஏணிகள் வருத்தமடைந்தனவோ?","explanation":"The poet is speaking about the refusal of a girl's father to give her in marriage to suitors who are not deemed worthy, despite their offering immense wealth. The poem describes the prosperous port city of Muciri, ruled by the Chera king Kuttuvan, where trade is bustling with fish, paddy, pepper, and gold. Despite suitors offering wealth comparable to Muciri's riches, the father refuses them because they lack nobility or worthiness. Consequently, the suitors prepare for war to take her by force, placing siege ladders against the fort walls. The poem belongs to the kañci tiṇai (specifically makaṭpāṟ kañci, where a father refuses to give his daughter to kings, leading to a siege). The contrast between the peaceful, prosperous trade of Muciri and the impending doom of a besieged town highlights the tragic pride of the father, while the image of kites sighing on the ramparts where ladders are pitched foreshadows the death and destruction of the coming battle.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}